-- title:
--   Two minimal primes in the geometric special fibre at p ∥ M
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $p$ and $M$ with $p$ prime and $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume $p \mid M$ but $p^{2} \nmid M$, together with the hypothesis `hHp` that every unit $u \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ whose image under the reduction map $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$ already lies in $H$, i.e. $H$ contains the kernel of that reduction. Assume further `hj`: the Laurent series $\mathrm{jqModC}\,\mathbb{Q} = q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}$-type integral power series, coefficients mapped to $\mathbb{Q})$ lies in `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the quotients of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for the full group $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ carrying an algebra structure over $R\,p$ (the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ at $p$). Write $\mathcal{O}$ for `chartAlgFin p (ΓM M H) hj`, the $j$-finite chart algebra of the two-chart integral model: the subalgebra of elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` that are integral over the $R\,p$-subalgebra generated by the element $j$ attached to `hj`. Then the set of minimal prime ideals of $\kappa \otimes_{R\,p} \mathcal{O}$ is finite, and its cardinality is exactly $2$.
--
--   This is the statement that the geometric special fibre at $p$ of the $j$-finite chart of the integral model of the modular curve of level `ΓM M H`, for $p$ exactly dividing $M$ and $H$ containing the kernel of reduction, has exactly two irreducible components — the Deligne–Rapoport picture of two copies of the lower-level curve crossing at the supersingular points. It feeds the construction of the pair of $q$-expansion readings and retractions at that level, and the vanishing statement for the associated retraction on the supersingular set.
